WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:03.290
Being a character actor's a pretty sweet deal.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:07.930
While they might not earn the fame, fortune,
or accolades afforded A-list movie stars,

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.290
some do get to live their dream and become
very well regarded for their work.

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:16.129
And there are other perks to the gig: like,
landing in a delightful, crowd-pleasing gag

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:17.129
reel.

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:20.790
Here are some performers who, at the end of
the day, are probably best loved for their

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:21.790
bloopers.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.860
Christopher Darga in Bruce Almighty

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:28.650
Jim Carrey improvises so much on set that
directors are left with a wealth of extra,

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.380
hilarious, and often unusable footage.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.500
This means that any day player who had a scene
with Carrey could also wind up in the gag

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.500
reel.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.260
That's what happened to Christopher Darga,
who played a baker in Bruce Almighty.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.740
"It must be wonderful seeing the smiles on
their little faces."

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.720
"I work in back.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.710
I see no smiles."

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:52.530
Darga was forever immortalized in film history
as a guy who can't keep a straight face...forever.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.050
"Oompa."

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.570
"Loompa."

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:57.090
"Doompa."

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.610
[Laughter]

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.280
"Oh, jeez."

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.380
Ken Foree in Halloween

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:08.290
Horror movies can provide a cathartic, psychological
release, but you have to laugh a little at

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:09.470
this tragic fate.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:14.180
And when actor Ken Foree did just that, he
provided perhaps his most famous screen work.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:19.820
"Hey buddy, just to give you a heads up: I
got a taco deluxe supreme talkin' back at

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:23.590
me, so I'ma be a while."

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:28.420
While filming his character's violent end
for 2007's remake of Halloween, Foree can't

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.320
help but find his stabbing rather humorous.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:38.990
[Grunting then laughter]

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:40.840
Some kid in North by Northwest

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.880
One of the most memorable outtakes from classic
cinema comes from Alfred Hitchcock's 1959

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.619
classic North by Northwest.

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:50.380
It includes one of Cary Grant's best performances...

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.330
"You know, I have that effect on people, it's
something about my face."

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.720
"It's a nice face."

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:01.299
...But the actor who really made history is
an anonymous child extra.

00:02:01.299 --> 00:02:05.730
Grant's costar, Eva Marie Saint, is about
to fire a gun in a crowded cafeteria, which

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:09.859
we know, from the kid in the background who
plugs his ears in anticipation.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.500
"You just stay away from me."

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.260
[Gunshots and screaming]

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.340
Paul Freeman in Raiders of the Lost Ark

00:02:18.359 --> 00:02:21.950
Character actor Paul Freeman appeared in one
of the most acclaimed and highest-grossing

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.829
blockbusters of all time.

00:02:24.829 --> 00:02:29.359
"I see your taste in friends remains consistent."

00:02:29.359 --> 00:02:34.420
But Freeman would become most famous for his
role as Belloq in 1981's Raiders of the Lost

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.519
Ark, because of a fly that crawled into his
mouth.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.780
"Your persistence surprises even me.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.160
[BUZZ, CHOMP]

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.510
You're gonna give mercenaries a bad name."

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.879
Soupy Sales in The Soupy Sales Show

00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:52.579
Unlike other iconic kiddie TV show hosts like
Captain Kangaroo or Mr. Rogers, Soupy Sales

00:02:52.579 --> 00:02:55.220
didn't run a cuddly educational show.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:59.560
Lunch with Soupy Sales, aka The Soupy Sales
Show, was pure comedy.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.739
For example, he took a pie to the face most
every day, and he used a stage door from where

00:03:03.739 --> 00:03:06.709
all manner of crazy guests would emerge.

00:03:06.709 --> 00:03:11.949
Perhaps because the show was light and ephemeral,
or perhaps because it wasn't rerun for decades,

00:03:11.949 --> 00:03:16.379
Sales is probably best remembered for a stage
door prank, where a topless dancer greets

00:03:16.379 --> 00:03:19.410
him by surprise — a gag which obviously
never hit the air.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:25.650
"Thank you for being with us, have a nice
evening and great day tomorrow, bye bye everybody."

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.599
Stanley Anderson in Spider-Man

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:31.849
Probably thanks to an extensive theatrical
background, Stanley Anderson projects a lot

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:37.139
of gravitas and hubris, which certainly helped
him win the role of General Slocum, an intimidating

00:03:37.139 --> 00:03:42.169
military official who could handle bossing
around Willem Dafoe in 2002's Spider-Man.

00:03:42.169 --> 00:03:45.540
But Anderson just couldn't get through the
word "predecessor," which means he'll live

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.419
on forever in the gag reel.

00:03:47.419 --> 00:03:49.879
"I never supported your program.

00:03:49.879 --> 00:03:52.969
We have my predess…

00:03:52.969 --> 00:03:54.799
[Gibberish]"

00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:56.829
Brian Steel in Blade: Trinity

00:03:56.829 --> 00:04:01.859
Even the biggest fan of Wesley Snipes' vampire-hunter
trilogy probably wouldn't recognize Brian

00:04:01.859 --> 00:04:02.859
Steele.

00:04:02.859 --> 00:04:07.760
In Blade: Trinity, he played the mighty Dracula,
which required layers of prosthetics and makeup.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.540
Steele was supposed to play his character's
death as an extremely violent one, but ended

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:15.689
up laughing his way through the outtakes.

00:04:15.689 --> 00:04:17.820
[Laughter]

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:18.360
"Cut."

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.160
Rachel Dratch as "Debbie Downer"

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:28.200
A remarkably talented comedian and actress,
Rachel Dratch, is best known for her seven-year

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.090
stint on Saturday Night Live.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:34.000
She performed several recurring characters,
but the piece for which Dratch will forever

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.350
be remembered is a Debbie Downer sketch that
went completely off the rails.

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:43.090
While portraying a family eating breakfast
at Disney World, almost the entire cast cracked

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.440
up.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:46.940
"By the way, it's official.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.360
I can't have children."

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:52.360
[Laughter]

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.880
Til Schweiger in Inglourious Basterds

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:59.860
While German writer, director, and actor Til
Schweiger is quite well-known in Europe, his

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:04.930
most memorable American screen appearance
was as Sargeant Stiglitz in 2009's Inglourious

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.040
Basterds.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:10.700
Arguably, Schweiger's best moment is when
he rises from the dead to say hello to Sally

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:15.160
Menke, the film's editor, and only person
who would see him come back to life.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.480
"Sally, I am not dead!

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.600
I just pretended.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:24.520
Now I'm gonna go after him and I'm gonna kick
his f---ing nazi balls ok?"

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.520
Thanks for watching!

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.750
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.949
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

